---
import MadeByKaj from '../components/MadeByKaj.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const explorePath = `${basePath}explore/`;
const teachPath = `${basePath}teach/`;
const learnBuildPath = `${basePath}learn-build/`;
const constellationFlyThroughPath = `${basePath}explore/constellations-and-3d-space/`;
const hrDiagramPath = `${basePath}learn/topic/hr-diagram/`;
const starterDataPath = `${basePath}build/download-the-star-data/`;
const aboutPath = `${basePath}about/`;
---

<Layout
	title="Found in Space"
	description="Found in Space turns open astronomical measurements into explorable 3D worlds: see what each view is made from, question the evidence, and build with it."
>
	<SiteHeader section="Learning through data" />

	<main class="page">
		<section class="hero home-hero">
			<p class="eyebrow">See it. Question it. Build with it.</p>
			<h1>Explore the nearby stars. Then look behind the view.</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				Found in Space starts with open astronomical measurements and turns them into
				interactive 3D experiences. Explore the view, see how it was made, ask what the
				evidence can and cannot show, and use the same data and code to build something of
				your own.
			</p>
			<div class="hero__actions" aria-label="Primary routes">
				<a class="button button--primary" href={explorePath}>Explore the stars</a>
				<a class="button button--ghost" href={teachPath}>Teach with Found in Space</a>
				<a class="button button--ghost" href={learnBuildPath}>Learn &amp; build with the data</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="route-grid" aria-label="Choose a route">
			<a class="panel panel--accent route-card" href={explorePath}>
				<p class="panel__eyebrow">Explore the stars</p>
				<h2>Start with wonder.</h2>
				<p>
					For anyone who wants to see the sky differently. Begin with familiar constellations,
					then move through 3D star positions estimated from catalogue measurements and watch
					the flat night sky open into depth.
				</p>
				<p class="route-card__meta">Best for: first-time visitors, visual exploration, public engagement</p>
				<span class="route-card__cta">Browse the visual journeys</span>
			</a>

			<a class="panel route-card" href={teachPath}>
				<p class="panel__eyebrow">Teach through inquiry</p>
				<h2>Turn visuals into inquiry.</h2>
				<p>
					For teachers, lecturers and workshop leaders. Use guided visualisations, classroom
					prompts and open-ended investigations to ask what the measurements show, what remains
					uncertain, and how the representation shapes what we notice.
				</p>
				<p class="route-card__meta">Best for: activities, workshops, outreach, student projects</p>
				<span class="route-card__cta">Open the teacher hub</span>
			</a>

			<a class="panel route-card" href={learnBuildPath}>
				<p class="panel__eyebrow">Learn &amp; build</p>
				<h2>Work with the data.</h2>
				<p>
					For students, pupils, curious coders and independent learners. Learn the astronomy and
					data concepts, inspect the pipeline, or use the open data and code to build your own
					visualisation, investigation or game.
				</p>
				<p class="route-card__meta">Best for: self-study, starter data, notebooks, code, projects</p>
				<span class="route-card__cta">Find a starting point</span>
			</a>
		</section>

		<section class="definition" aria-label="What is Found in Space?">
			<div class="definition__copy">
				<p class="eyebrow">What is Found in Space?</p>
				<h2>Part planetarium, part classroom, part open science lab.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="definition__body">
				<p>
					Found in Space begins with measurements from Gaia, Hipparcos and other catalogues. It
					lets people explore the resulting view while keeping visible how those measurements
					were selected, estimated and turned into a 3D world.
				</p>
				<p>
					A scientific picture might be built from observations, derived measurements, models,
					simulations or illustration. They can all be useful, but they are not the same. The aim
					is to make those layers clear and explorable, so people can ask what each one can—and
					cannot—tell us.
				</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="proof" aria-label="What the project includes">
				<ul class="proof__list">
					<li>Open astronomical measurements and derived data</li>
					<li>Interactive 3D browser visualisations</li>
					<li>Explanations of sources, assumptions and limitations</li>
					<li>Guided questions and open-ended investigations</li>
					<li>Open data pipeline, viewer and reusable code</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

		<section class="start-points" aria-label="Suggested first steps">
			<article class="panel">
				<p class="panel__eyebrow">See it</p>
				<h2>Constellations and 3D space</h2>
				<p>
					Start with Orion and see how a familiar sky pattern changes when each star is placed at
					its estimated distance.
				</p>
				<a class="link--gold" href={constellationFlyThroughPath}>Open the fly-through</a>
			</article>
			<article class="panel">
				<p class="panel__eyebrow">Question it</p>
				<h2>The HR diagram</h2>
				<p>
					Plot temperature against luminosity, then ask what the structure tells you and what the
					sample might be hiding.
				</p>
				<a class="link--gold" href={hrDiagramPath}>Open the lesson</a>
			</article>
			<article class="panel">
				<p class="panel__eyebrow">Build with it</p>
				<h2>Build something visible</h2>
				<p>
					Begin with a small bright-star data guide before deciding whether to run the full
					pipeline yourself.
				</p>
				<a class="link--gold" href={starterDataPath}>Open the guide</a>
			</article>
		</section>

		<section class="about-teaser" aria-label="About the project">
			<p>
				Found in Space is not just a star viewer. It is a way to see what the view is made
				from, ask what it can tell us, and build with the material behind it.
			</p>
			<a class="button button--ghost" href={aboutPath}>About the project</a>
		</section>

		<MadeByKaj />
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page {
		position: relative;
		min-height: 100vh;
	}

	.home-hero {
		max-width: 58rem;
		padding-top: 4.5rem;
		padding-bottom: 3.5rem;
	}

	h1,
	h2,
	h3 {
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0;
	}

	h1 {
		max-width: 13ch;
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 4.8rem;
		line-height: 1;
	}

	h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
		font-size: 1.7rem;
		line-height: 1.12;
		color: var(--fis-text);
	}

	p {
		margin: 0;
		line-height: 1.7;
		color: var(--fis-text-soft);
	}

	p + p {
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	.hero__actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.85rem;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.button--ghost {
		background: var(--fis-panel);
	}

	.route-grid,
	.start-points {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.route-grid {
		margin: 0 0 4rem;
	}

	.route-card {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		min-height: 24rem;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition:
			border-color 160ms ease,
			transform 160ms ease;
	}

	.route-card:hover {
		border-color: var(--fis-line-strong);
		transform: translateY(-3px);
	}

	.route-card__meta {
		margin-top: 1.2rem;
		font-family: var(--fis-font-ui);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		color: var(--fis-text-muted);
	}

	.route-card__cta {
		display: block;
		margin-top: auto;
		padding-top: 1.4rem;
		color: var(--fis-gold);
		font-family: var(--fis-font-ui);
		font-size: 0.94rem;
	}

	.definition {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
		gap: 3rem;
		padding: 4rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--fis-line);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--fis-line);
	}

	.definition h2 {
		max-width: 15ch;
		font-size: 2.4rem;
		line-height: 1.06;
	}

	.definition__body {
		max-width: 42rem;
		font-size: 1.12rem;
	}

	.proof {
		padding: 2rem 0 3.4rem;
	}

	.proof__list {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.7rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
	}

	.proof__list li {
		padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--fis-blue-subtle);
		border-radius: 999px;
		background: var(--fis-panel);
		color: var(--fis-text-soft);
		font-family: var(--fis-font-ui);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}

	.start-points {
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
	}

	.start-points .panel {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.7rem;
	}

	.start-points a {
		margin-top: auto;
		padding-top: 0.6rem;
	}

	.about-teaser {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1.5rem;
		margin-bottom: 4rem;
		padding: 1.5rem 0 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--fis-line);
	}

	.about-teaser p {
		max-width: 42rem;
		font-size: 1.2rem;
		color: var(--fis-text);
	}

	@media (max-width: 960px) {
		h1 {
			font-size: 3.8rem;
		}

		.route-grid,
		.start-points,
		.definition {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.route-card {
			min-height: auto;
		}

		.definition {
			gap: 1.5rem;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.home-hero {
			padding-top: 2.5rem;
		}

		h1 {
			font-size: 3rem;
		}

		.hero__actions,
		.about-teaser {
			align-items: stretch;
			flex-direction: column;
		}

		.hero__actions .button,
		.about-teaser .button {
			width: 100%;
		}
	}
</style>
